        "<b>Autonomic dysreflexia</b> (lesions at or above about T6): sit up, loosen clothing, check bladder/bowel, monitor BP, get help.",
        "<b>Parkinson</b>: external cues, high-amplitude training. <b>MS</b>: avoid heat, rest intervals. <b>MG</b>: exercise at medication peak, rest breaks. <b>ALS</b>: avoid overwork, conserve energy.",
        "<b>BPPV</b>: Dix-Hallpike; posterior canal = upbeating torsional nystagmus; treat with canalith repositioning.",
        "<b>Vestibular hypofunction</b>: gaze stabilization (VOR x1), habituation, balance training."
